Let E be a real inner-product space, let κ be a nonempty finite index type, let Σ : E → E be a continuous linear operator, let x : κ → E, and let B ≥ 0. Assume Σ is symmetric, ‖Σ‖ ≤ B², and ‖x_i‖ ≤ B for every i ∈ κ. Define M̂ = |κ|⁻¹ ∑_{i∈κ} x_i ⊗ x_i. Then
M̂ − Σ = |κ|⁻¹ ∑_{i∈κ} (x_i ⊗ x_i − Σ);
for every i ∈ κ, x_i ⊗ x_i − Σ is symmetric; and for every i ∈ κ,
‖x_i ⊗ x_i − Σ‖ ≤ 2B²,
where (x_i ⊗ x_i)(y) = ⟨x_i, y⟩x_i.
